    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nFiles\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nUsing MiniFiles will give a spurious \"Title requires border to be set\" on occasions, more specifically when navigating to the parent directory. This also happens consistently after opening and closing man page(s).\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev+2428-g7e008799a\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `Open help page (F1)`\r\n3. `Quit help page`\r\n4. `Open MiniFiles`\r\n5. `Navigate to parent directory (H)`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n[Screencast from 2024-02-24 10-14-25.webm](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/2d8842ea-3874-4096-ac18-c510d52b0960)\r\n",
