            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Thanks for the issue!\r\n> \r\n> Unfortunately, I can not reproduce. Did you actually try it with minimal config, i.e. at least with `nvim -u NONE` and loading only 'mini.files'?\r\n\r\nMy bad, indeed I couldn't reproduce it with a clean setup, so I dissected everything to find the cause. It happens when using wincmd L in a filetype autocmd for help page. That is:\r\n\r\n> after/ftplugin/help.lua\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({\r\n  [[BufWinEnter]],\r\n}, {\r\n  desc = [[Use vertical split for help pages.]],\r\n  callback = function(event)\r\n    vim.api.nvim_exec2 ([[wincmd L]], {})\r\n  end\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `Open help page (F1)`\r\n3. `Quit help page`\r\n4. `Open MiniFiles`\r\n5. `Navigate to parent directory (H)`",
